{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And his family.</b> Rabbi Shimon said: but what sin did the family commit? Rather, this teaches you that there is no family that has a molech-worshipper in it where they are not all practitioners — for they all cover for him (Sifra; Shevuot 39)." "<b>And I will cut him off.</b> Why is this stated? Since it is said <b>and his family</b>, one might think the whole family would be in excision — Scripture says אֹתוֹ — him in excision, and not the whole family in excision, but rather through suffering (ibid.)." "<b>To go whoring after the molech.</b> To include other forms of idolatry that he worshipped in this manner, even if this is not its [normal] mode of worship (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:23.515100581Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}